# py_doctor

Diagnose and fix your FastAPI project health - Python equivalent of flutter_doctor.

## Installation

### Recommended — uv tool (no venv needed)

git clone https://github.com/yourname/py_doctor
cd py_doctor
./tool/activate.sh

### Alternative — uv pip

uv pip install git+https://github.com/yourname/py_doctor

### Alternative — pip

pip install py-doctor

## Usage on any FastAPI project

# No venv activation needed — just run:

py_doctor /path/to/your/fastapi/project --verbose

# Or from inside the project:

cd /path/to/your/fastapi/project
py_doctor . --verbose
py_doctor . --score
py_doctor . --no-md

## Config (optional) — add to your project

Create py_doctor.config.json in your FastAPI project root:
{
"ignore": {
"rules": ["bandit/B404", "ruff/E501"],
"files": ["migrations/", "tests/", "alembic/"]
}
}

Or in pyproject.toml:
[tool.py_doctor.ignore]
rules = ["bandit/B404", "ruff/E501"]
files = ["migrations/", "tests/"]

## CLI Usage

```
py_doctor .                        # scan current directory
py_doctor . --verbose              # show file:line per rule
py_doctor . --score                # output score only for CI
py_doctor . --no-lint              # skip lint pass
# ... full usage from spec
```

See terminal output example in project spec.

## Config

pyproject.toml [tool.py_doctor] or py_doctor.config.json
